                <pb facs="0138" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg42"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/2838a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Young</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-26T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                                1926—8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>31. Before approving the proposed Dominican loan in any amount the Department is
                    anxious to feel assured that the money destined for public works will be wisely
                    and efficiently expended. The Department understands that one of the conditions
                    for the bidders on the aqueduct project was that a surety company would execute
                    a performance bond in the sum of $300,000 guaranteeing satisfactory completion
                    of the contract. The Department feels that this was a wise precaution on the
                    part of the Dominican Government and trusts that this condition will be insisted
                    upon. You may informally advise the President of the above and state further
                    that the Department can approve a loan to the Dominican Government for
                    construction of public works only if the Department is satisfied that these
                    works will be undertaken by reliable and experienced companies.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
